# Normative specification

`spec/` is the authoritative source for intended product behavior.

## Structure

- `product.md` — product purpose, boundaries and normative behavior
- `requirements/` — atomic requirements
- `capabilities/` — product capabilities and their requirements
- `flows/` — machine-readable behavioral flows
- `schema/` — schemas for machine-readable specification artifacts

IDs use the project prefix `[[ spec_prefix ]]`:

- `[[ spec_prefix ]]-REQ-*`
- `[[ spec_prefix ]]-CAP-*`
- `[[ spec_prefix ]]-FLOW-*`

Source code and tests must implement and verify the specification.

Exploratory material does not belong here. Use `project-memory/`.

Architectural rationale belongs in `docs/decisions/`.
